    "text": "Suppose that a subgroup H of a finite group G is such that HM = M H for\nevery minimal non-nilpotent subgroup M of G. Must H/HG be nilpotent, where HG\nis the largest normal subgroup of G contained in H? V. N. Knyagina, V. S. Monakhov\n  ∗ No, not always (A. Ballester-Bolinches, R. Esteban-Romero, S. F. Kamornikov,\nV. Pérez-Calabuig, J. Algebra, 608 (2022), 382–387).",
